# `nestjs/no-test-outside-describe`

The rule reports an `it` / `test` that is outside every `describe`, or written directly in the outermost suite `describe`. It counts nesting. It does not read titles.

When resolving `nestjs/no-test-outside-describe`:

1. Inspect the test and its surrounding suite.
2. Use the `fix-nestjs-test-outside-describe` skill to nest the test below the suite.
3. Use the `nestjs-test-grammar` skill to name the nested `describe`. Prefer a subject or thematic group when there is no real condition to extract. A nested `describe` does not have to start with `when`.
4. Split the test title only when a scenario `describe` now carries a condition that would be duplicated in the title — not for structural nesting alone. Do not replay `nestjs/no-when-in-test-title` unless that rule also applies.
5. Preserve the behavior the test exercises and observes.

Do not add a `describe` merely to satisfy the lint rule.

Do not manufacture a `when` scenario or pull context from fixture literals when the original title already states the behavioral outcome or category.

Leave unrelated test-quality issues to their own rules and skills.
